{"kind":"event","event_id":6910,"event_uid":"01M2NKZF69QYMS59MCBYBT2T9Z","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":296,"issue_uid":"01M2NKWNM2Q0S5KK3YFTXJKT94","issue_short_id":"kt94","actor":"impl:1@run-162","hlc_physical_ms":1789579476169,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"cb2b4f33083ce69f6702d14dbaf0b6aeea5a837fd1714bc66946160a637bd520","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NKZF68JWGJWNH2HCGV8BN4","author":"impl:1@run-162","body":"Task 1 approach: add two module-scope exports beside patchPaths/touchSetOf in fleet/run-engine.mjs — producedSymbolOf(entry) restating compile_plan.py's _interface_token, and addedExportsOf(patchFile) scanning a captured unified diff for added top-level export declarations (.mjs/.js/.ts/.tsx/.cjs/.mts) and column-zero def/class (.py). Then a collision scan at the tail of prePass (after the handshake push) that reads WAVES.flat() for sibling Produces tokens, pushes one red per distinct (name,path) and appends one driver:finding at round 0 via appendEvent. CONTRACT.md gets the collision sentence appended to the 'three more kinds' paragraph, before 'One more kind records'.","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:24:36.168251612Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:24:36.169Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":6921,"event_uid":"01M2NM654XGN760NMJ4XC4YRYB","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":296,"issue_uid":"01M2NKWNM2Q0S5KK3YFTXJKT94","issue_short_id":"kt94","actor":"exam:1@run-162","hlc_physical_ms":1789579695261,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"dcdd5e471acd5247b0d0cfb703da240b03e7636eed8d46d129a2180741aaa242","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NM654WTH4R074AH7QYQEXT","author":"exam:1@run-162","body":"examiner (round 1): approach for `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_export_collision.mjs`.\n\nTen `producedSymbolOf` equalities for leg (a) (verified against the compiler's own `_interface_token` at `skills/ultrapowers/scripts/compile_plan.py:1667`, so the engine's copy is pinned to the compiler's answers, not to my reading of them); one hand-written unified diff fixture for leg (b), asserted with a full `deepEqual` of the four rows in order plus `[]` for an unreadable path.\n\nLegs (c), (d), (e) stand real two-task runs on the shared `_engine_helpers.mjs` rig (`waves: [[A, B]]`, `width: 2`, `foldAgeMs: 0`), A Produces `receiptPaths`, B Produces `none`, B's implementer writing `b.mjs`. Probed at BASE: that run dispatches `impl:A, impl:B, review:A:1, review:B:1`, appends no `driver:finding`, and both rows are `done` — so the collision legs are red at BASE for exactly one reason (no `fix:B:0`, no finding).\n\nTwo readings I had to settle:\n\n1. The two new helpers are imported as a namespace (`import * as engine`) and their exportedness asserted, rather than as named imports. A named import of a symbol BASE does not export is a link-time SyntaxError that takes the whole file down, and legs (g)/(h) — which do not depend on the helpers at all — would never run. The namespace form keeps every leg reporting for itself while still failing at BASE on the absent export.\n\n2. Leg (f) names the second `Run:` (the whole `test_run_engine_proof_runs.mjs` sim), and `test_sims_are_hermetic.mjs` M4 forbids one `test_*.mjs` spawning another, so this file cannot run that sim itself. The driver runs it as the Proof's own second `Run:`; in-file, leg (f)'s M5 claim is pinned directly instead — one M5 run carries a `Run:` command and a Global Constraints `Check:`, and the exam asserts the exact ordered `driver:proof-run`/`driver:check-run`/`driver:exam-run` rows per task (one each at `iter: 0`, exit 0, no exam row) that BASE records.\n\n`evidence.against` is asserted against B's first captured `headSha`, read off the clone in the `impl:B` stub arm (the sims never commit, so that is the sha `withPatchCapture` records).","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:28:15.260014643Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:28:15.261Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":6936,"event_uid":"01M2NMD0XZ3HVJTHG1JG59EXWG","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":296,"issue_uid":"01M2NKWNM2Q0S5KK3YFTXJKT94","issue_short_id":"kt94","actor":"impl:1@run-162","hlc_physical_ms":1789579920319,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"5f595c91896c6d23d811602207d14212f6623402e437ca77b853aaa06aef1c8a","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NMD0XY1YWR4B3JFJQCHCV5","author":"impl:1@run-162","body":"Done and green on all six proofs. Two decisions a later session would otherwise rediscover:\n\n1. producedSymbolOf uses the compiler's FULL _DECL_KEYWORDS set (class, def, async, function, const, let, var, interface, type, struct, enum, export, abstract, static), not the eight M1 enumerates. A differential run against skills/ultrapowers/scripts/compile_plan.py's _interface_token over 25 entries agrees on all 25; with only M1's eight it disagreed on four (`interface Shape`, `type Row = …`, `abstract class Zed`, `static helper()` — the engine would have tokened them to the keyword and been blind to a real collision). The Claim's own sentence is 'exactly as the compiler does' and the Context says M1 restates it 'so the engine and the compiler agree', so agreement won over the enumeration. Declared as an amends: clause row.\n\n2. The backtick branch terminates on '(' , '->', '=', whitespace, ':' or the closing backtick — M1's rule, which is stricter than the compiler's split on [(\\\\s:] alone. The two only diverge on degenerate entries like `a->b`; M1 spells the stricter one so that is what is implemented.\n\nThe collision scan is the last thing prePass does, after the handshake push, so a pass that finds nothing records exactly what it recorded at BASE.","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:32:00.318434599Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:32:00.319Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":6937,"event_uid":"01M2NMDCFG4YXJ95RGMMEDYBNX","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":296,"issue_uid":"01M2NKWNM2Q0S5KK3YFTXJKT94","issue_short_id":"kt94","actor":"exam:1@run-162","hlc_physical_ms":1789579932144,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"b8108ecc6b90e8edb9634e836a5e515c0b1546057d5b2e0cffed7b78c355bcc3","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NMDCFFVDHK7RHWSVG5ZXMR","author":"exam:1@run-162","body":"examiner (round 1): exam handed in at `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_export_collision.mjs`, whole, at the guarded path.\n\nCoverage: leg (a) ten `producedSymbolOf` equalities; (b) one `deepEqual` of the four `addedExportsOf` rows in order over a hand-written diff carrying the removed/context/non-export/indented-`def` cases and the `+++ b/…` header, plus `[]` for an unreadable path; (c) the collision run — one `driver:finding` at `round` 0 with every field asserted by equality (including `detail` verbatim and `evidence` as a whole object), the `fix:B:0` dispatch carrying the line, the `impl:B` → `fix:B:0` → `review:B:1` order, B `done`, A untouched; (d) the stubborn fix — no `review:B:`, row `failed`/`proof-red`/notes, two findings, one per pass; (e) four runs (own-token, unrelated name, removed-line-only with a precondition read off the captured patch itself, single-task plan); (f) the exact ordered `driver:proof-run`/`driver:check-run` rows per task on the M5 run that carries a `Run:` and a `Check:`; (g) the CONTRACT.md range; (h) the file's own import lines.\n\nVerified both ways. At BASE it is red on the first assertion — `fleet/run-engine.mjs` exports no `producedSymbolOf` — and nothing else. Against a throwaway implementation of M1/M2/M3 and the M6 sentence (written in this tree, run, then reverted; the tree hands in the exam file alone) it prints `ALL TESTS PASSED` in ~3 s, and `test_run_engine_proof_runs.mjs` and `test_sims_are_hermetic.mjs` stayed green beside it.\n\nNothing unsatisfiable. The one substitution I did NOT make: leg (f) names the second `Run:`, which is the `Run:`-proofs sim, and this file may not spawn it (hermetic M4) — so the driver runs it as the Proof says, and what this file carries for (f) is M5's own sentence about the three row kinds, asserted on rows a real `Run:` and a real `Check:` produced, not a re-run of the other sim under another name.","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:32:12.143598078Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:32:12.144Z"}
